DEVIATIONS (honesty covenant rule 9 — surfaced, not silent)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The prompt generator collided two DISTINCT web components onto one native basename:

  web components/ui/ConfirmDialog.tsx  -> P-0012 -> native ConfirmDialog.*   (destructive dialog)
  web components/ai/ConfirmDialog.tsx  -> P-0001 -> native ConfirmDialog.*   (THIS task, AI dialog)

HEAD already ships the 0012 (ui, destructive) implementation at ConfirmDialog.* (10 files,
self-identified "P4 modal/dialog · 0012", parity of components/ui/ConfirmDialog.tsx — typed
confirmation + "Don't ask again" + severity variants). The 0001 (ai) surface is ABSENT from HEAD
(it was clobbered by 0012 in the original parallel merge — see the prior BLOCKED run logs
parallel/artifact-…-0199-P-0001 and -0210-P-0012).

Overwriting ConfirmDialog.* with the AI dialog would DESTROY the completed 0012 sibling surface
(violates honesty covenant rule 2 "No scope narrowing" + the repo integrity standards). The two are
different dialogs that both exist in the app. Resolution, to ship the AI parity WITHOUT regressing
the sibling:

  • Filename: AiConfirmDialog.*  (the web component is literally exported as `AiConfirmDialog`; the
    repo already uses descriptive dialog prefixes — CommandConfirmDialog.*, AcknowledgeAlertDialog.*).
  • Slug:     AiConfirmDialog   (the prompt's literal `ConfirmDialog` slug is already owned by 0012;
    a unique slug keeps the two surfaces unambiguous in diagnostics).
  • i18n keys are UNCHANGED from the web source (ai.confirm.* — already namespaced, no 0012 clash).

These two name changes are forced by the generator collision; everything else follows the prompt.

